/*!
 * comrade_jni::api — the Dart/Flutter FFI boundary, generated by
 * flutter_rust_bridge (FRB) v2.
 *
 * This is the *second* foreign ABI exported from this one cdylib. It is a
 * peer of, not a replacement for, the uniffi surface in [`crate`]: Kotlin's
 * background services (`WakeWordService`, `RelayConnectionService`,
 * `ModelDownloadService`, `CommandDispatcher`) must be able to reach Rust
 * without waking the Flutter engine, so they keep calling the uniffi
 * bindings, while the UI calls these functions from Dart.
 *
 * # One runtime, not two
 *
 * Every function here resolves [`crate::global_runtime`] — the same
 * `Arc<RwLock<ComradeRuntime>>` that `crate::Comrade` holds. That is load
 * bearing, not tidiness: `comrade_storage::EncryptedStore::open` opens the
 * vault with `redb::Database::create`, and redb takes an exclusive file lock,
 * so a second `ComradeRuntime` unlocking the same directory fails outright.
 * See `docs/FRONTEND_STRATEGY.md` §4 D2 and this crate's module header.
 *
 * # Sync vs async, and why it matters here
 *
 * FRB runs a plain `fn` on its own worker thread pool and an `async fn` on its
 * own Tokio runtime. `ComradeRuntime`'s cheap accessors use
 * `RwLock::blocking_read`/`blocking_write`, which **panic** if called from
 * inside a Tokio reactor — so those stay plain `fn` (a worker thread has no
 * ambient reactor, exactly like the JNA thread the uniffi tier is called on),
 * and only the methods that genuinely need a reactor are `async fn`. The
 * split below is deliberately identical to the one in [`crate::Comrade`].
 *
 * `#[frb(sync)]` — which runs the body *on the Dart isolate thread*, blocking
 * it — is used only for the handful of pure, allocation-cheap helpers that
 * touch no runtime state at all.
 *
 * # Regenerating the bindings
 *
 * `src/frb_generated.rs` and the Dart side are produced by:
 *
 * ```text
 * flutter_rust_bridge_codegen generate \
 *   --rust-input crate::api \
 *   --rust-root crates/comrade_jni \
 *   --dart-output <flutter-app>/lib/src/rust \
 *   --no-add-mod-to-lib --no-web
 * ```
 *
 * `--no-add-mod-to-lib` because `mod frb_generated;` is already declared by
 * hand in lib.rs, next to `uniffi::setup_scaffolding!`. The Dart package needs
 * `flutter_rust_bridge` + `freezed_annotation` as dependencies and
 * `build_runner` + `freezed` as dev-dependencies — the bridged enums
 * (`BridgeEvent`, `CallSignal`, `UiError`) generate freezed unions, and
 * codegen refuses to finish without them.
 *
 * The mirror declarations below exist because FRB only bridges types it can
 * see in the crate it parses; the DTOs live in `comrade_ui`/`comrade_core`.
 * They are a straight field-for-field restatement — **if you add a field to a
 * DTO, add it here too**, or codegen will fail with a field mismatch.
 */

